# Project-specific
dev_note/github_issues.md
.binder/
# `.github/` used to be ignored wholesale, which made CI impossible to add: a
# workflow file that git cannot see never reaches GitHub and never runs. That is
# also why `.github/workflows/docs.yml` is in the repository only because someone
# `git add -f`'d it. A *directory* rule cannot be undone by a negation (see the
# note below the asset patterns), so the local-only assistant scaffolding is
# listed explicitly and `.github/workflows/` stays visible.
.github/agents/
.github/chatmodes/
.github/prompts/
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.specify/
.local/
specs/

script/*.ipynb
!script/run_ueler.ipynb
!script/run_ueler_binder.ipynb
site/

CLAUDE.md
.claude/
graphify-out/
*.png

# Assets that ship in the wheel or render in the docs must survive the blanket
# *.txt / *.png rules above. setuptools builds from the working tree, so an
# ignored asset is present in a local build and silently missing from one made
# on a clean checkout (CI, or a fresh clone) — a wheel that only breaks for
# users. Negations must stay below the patterns they override: last match wins.
!LICENSE.txt
!ueler/**/*.png
!doc/**/*.png
!docs/**/*.png